      },
      "hints": [
        "Use the relations between roots and coefficients for $px^2 + 4x - 5 = 0$: sum of roots is $-\\frac{4}{p}$ and product of roots is $-\\frac{5}{p}$.",
        "Equate the sum $5m + (-9m) = -4m = -\\frac{4}{p}$ to find $p = \\frac{1}{m}$.",
        "Equate the product $(5m)(-9m) = -45m^2 = -\\frac{5}{p}$ to solve for $m$ and $p$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the sum of roots for the quadratic equation $px^2 + 4x - 5 = 0$:\n$$\\text{Sum of roots: } 5m + (-9m) = -4m = -\\frac{4}{p} \\implies m = \\frac{1}{p} \\implies p = \\frac{1}{m}$$",
        "Use the product of roots:\n$$\\text{Product of roots: } (5m)(-9m) = -45m^2 = -\\frac{5}{p}$$",
        "Substitute $p = \\frac{1}{m}$ into the product equation:\n$$-45m^2 = -5m \\implies 45m^2 = 5m$$",
        "Divide by $m$ (since roots are non-zero, $m \\neq 0$) and solve for $m$ and $p$:\n$$45m = 5 \\implies m = \\frac{5}{45} = \\frac{1}{9}$$\n$$p = \\frac{1}{m} = 9$$"
      ],
